A circular fountain has the diameter marked. Write its exact circumference, in terms of $\pi$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\begin{scope}[shift={(0,0)}]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.6);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw (0,0)--(50:1.6) node[midway,above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$15\text{ mm}$};
\node[below] at (0,-2.15) {Circle A};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(4.60,0)}]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.5);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (180:1.5)--(0:1.5) node[midway,below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$2.8\text{ cm}$};
\node[below] at (0,-2.05) {Circle B};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which circle has the larger circumference, and what are the two circumferences in millimetres, correct to $2$ decimal places?
